Leste's patches/libssc-wakeup-batching.patch (scripts/46-sensor-stack.sh), the same for FreeBSD.

The sensor core's power-saving delivery for libssc (docs/sensors.md):
non-waking delivery and batching in every enable request (the batch spec
and suspend mode of the sensor core's client API, which libssc's protocol
had as "unknown" field 1 and a fixed WAKEUP), set per sensor
(ssc_sensor_set_delivery) or system-wide in libssc.conf; flush requests
(ssc_sensor_flush) and reconfiguring an open sensor (ssc_sensor_reconfigure);
the step counter's real step event (1028) besides the count on a request
(775), flush and error events no longer read as counts; ssccli --batch-ms,
--no-wakeup, --flush-only, --flush-every, --probe. Without libssc.conf and
without a client's own setting the requests are byte for byte those of
before. Applies after libssc-pedometer.patch and libssc-sync-wait.patch.

diff --git a/data/ssc-common.proto b/data/ssc-common.proto
index 87c89a3..f539f3a 100644
--- a/data/ssc-common.proto
+++ b/data/ssc-common.proto
@@ -32,21 +32,42 @@ message SscUid {
  * Client configuration 
  * @processor: a value from the SscProcessorType enum. Default APPS (1).
  * @suspend_mode: a value from the SscSuspendType enum. Default WAKEUP (0).
+ *   WAKEUP (0): events are sent as they become due, also to a suspended
+ *   processor. NO_WAKEUP (1): while the processor is suspended the sensor
+ *   core keeps the events (it may drop the oldest periodic ones when its
+ *   buffer is full) and sends them once the processor is awake again.
  * @no_wakeup_msg_ids: list of messages that do not cause a wakeup.
  */
 message SscClientConfig {
         required int32 processor = 1 [default = 1];
         required int32 suspend_mode = 2 [default = 0]; 
+        repeated fixed32 no_wakeup_msg_ids = 3;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Batching of a request
+ * @batch_period: microseconds an event may wait in the sensor core before
+ *   it is sent, so that several go out in one report; 0: no batching.
+ * @flush_period: microseconds of events the sensor core keeps at least
+ *   (older ones may be dropped); default: batch_period plus a margin.
+ * @flush_only: send only on a flush request or when the buffer is full.
+ * @max_batch: batch at the sensor core's full capacity.
+ */
+message SscBatchSpec {
+	required uint32 batch_period = 1;
+	optional uint32 flush_period = 2;
+	optional bool flush_only = 3 [default = false];
+	optional bool max_batch = 4 [default = false];
 }
 
 /*
  * Client request body
- * @unknown: optional
+ * @batching: batching of the events of this request, none by default.
  * @msg: the actual sensor request, specific for each sensor.
  * @is_passive: request is passive or not. Active triggers sensor activation.
  */
 message SscClientRequestBody {
-	optional bytes unknown = 1;
+	optional SscBatchSpec batching = 1;
 	optional bytes msg = 2;
 	optional bool is_passive = 3 [default = false];
 }
